"Ask new members to confirm their email address. Choose how strictly it is "
"enforced below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1586 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2433
msgid "How strictly to enforce verification"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1587
msgid ""
"Restricted (recommended): members can look around but cannot post or comment "
"until they confirm. Full: they cannot use the community at all until they "
"confirm."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1594 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2388
msgid "Require members to accept your terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1595 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2389
msgid "Shows a consent checkbox on every sign-up route. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1602 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2399
msgid "Ask new members for their name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1603 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2400
msgid ""
"On by default. This is the name other members see. Turn it off only if your "
"community wants handles rather than names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1610 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2406
msgid "Let members choose their own username"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1611 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2407
msgid ""
"Off by default: a username is generated from their email so nobody has to "
"invent one to join, and they can change it later in Settings. Turn this on "
"to ask for one at sign-up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1618 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2413
msgid "Also allow the WordPress sign-up form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1619 includes/Admin/Settings.php:2414
msgid ""
"Off by default: wp-login.php sign-ups are sent to your BuddyNext sign-up "
"page instead. Turn this on if another plugin relies on the WordPress form. "
"It is protected by your settings either way."
msgstr ""

